final.verdict:
Compile: no blocker found. Neither the three reviews nor my full re-read found anything MetaEditor should reject:
- the CTrade calls match a 2000-2025 Trade.mqh, which itself declares a local `int exp`;
- the CopyRates overloads, all 11 StringFormat calls and the brackets check out;
- R1's line-660 casts and line-296 sign-mismatch remark are at most warnings.
No compiler was run, so the first F7 build in MetaEditor is still the real test.

Trading: NOT safe. The six P1 fixes (F1-F6) cover wrong alerts or trades in normal operation:
- mode 1 manages nothing;
- the replay flag fires at every market closure, leaves the Sunday-open window without mode-2 orders and sends about 2 bogus pushes a day;
- the demo-only guard can be bypassed at terminal start (new finding, plausible), and terminals share one state file;
- a stale real ticket silently kills the mode-0 paper engine;
- leftover GTC orders and the never-written 'virtual entry' make mode 2 diverge from the paper.

P2 (F7-F13) covers outages, broker refusals, history sync, the integrity of the mandatory tester parity check, and the minimum-spread ask. P3 (F14-F21) covers rare or low-impact defects. For mode 0 observation, the minimum is F2, F3, F4 and F12. Modes 1 and 2 need all of P1 and P2.

Dropped after verification:
- line-660 casts and the line-296 warning (both compile);
- ResetLastError before WebRequest (diagnostic only);
- SetTypeFillingBySymbol and deviation (CTrade's FillingCheck already picks FOK or IOC);
- DeletePendings at line 456 (unreachable while br_active is 1);
- line 784 closing a legitimate fill (unreachable after F4/F5; F20 adds a guard anyway);
- a CASSURE alert on old levels in a window's first minute (the new levels lie inside the old ones);
- deleting GTC orders at the Friday close (a Sunday-gap fill gets the same price and deadline as the paper);
- Build4H vs max bars (3,648 M5 bars are enough);
- holiday time-exit rule, ATR seeding, tester warm start, early Decide and Decide break/retry (zero or negligible measured impact);
- netting, the refused-mode Print, binder volume and scale-in checks, message wording, heartbeat push, and TimeGMT stamps in the tester (UX or documentation only).

Rejected fix variants: R1's file key read in OnInit (the state would be lost on every restart), and R2's bar-age and R3's boot-time replay rules (see F2).

Reference implementation: all 21 fixes are applied together in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-gold-orb/340d9f5a-4d28-5733-90cb-10a10699d00b/scratchpad/patch/GoldOrb_Donchian4H_fixed.mq5. Lint: brackets balanced, 14 of 14 StringFormat calls match, pure ASCII, no duplicate definitions; it has NOT been compiled. The fixed checker is /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-gold-orb/340d9f5a-4d28-5733-90cb-10a10699d00b/scratchpad/patch/compare_journal_fixed.py.

Final handler order:
- OnTick: AccountReady gate, CatchUp, BindManualPosition, VirtualEntry, TickTrigger, RealTimeExit.
- OnTimer: AccountReady gate, CatchUp, BindManualPosition, RealTimeExit, Reconcile every 60 s, Housekeeping, FlushPush, FlushTelegram.

No repository file was modified.
